+---
+title: "Testing click.utils to 100% line+branch coverage"
+author: HarzerHeribert
+date: 2026-10-15
+cost: { minutes: 2, tokens: 34127 }
+touches:
+  - tests/test_utils/test_utils_more.py
+  - src/click/utils.py
+---
+
+## Decided
+- tests/test_utils/test_utils_more.py takes src/click/utils.py to 100% line and branch coverage without touching src/.
+- Platform branches in `get_app_dir` are reached by monkeypatching `click.utils.WIN` (a module constant, so patch it on click.utils) and `sys.platform`, plus the APPDATA, LOCALAPPDATA and XDG_CONFIG_HOME env vars. Patch `WIN=False` explicitly so the non-Windows tests also pass on Windows CI.
+- `_detect_program_name()` with no arguments is made deterministic with `monkeypatch.setitem(sys.modules, "__main__", fake_module)` and `monkeypatch.setattr(sys, "argv", ...)`.
+- `_LazyFile("-", "w")`, `_get_text_stream` and `_get_binary_stream` are tested by monkeypatching `sys.stdout` to a StringIO, or to a TextIOWrapper over BytesIO, instead of relying on pytest's capture stream.
+
+## Tried and ruled out
+- Triggering `re.error` in `_expand_args` with a "bad" glob pattern does not work: modern `fnmatch.translate` escapes everything. Monkeypatch `glob.glob` instead. `_expand_args` imports it inside the function, so patching the module attribute works.
+
+## Watch out
+- pytest runs with `filterwarnings = ["error"]`: unclosed files (ResourceWarning) and deprecated `click.utils.<public alias>` access fail tests. Use the `_private` names directly.
+- `echo`'s "bytes but no binary writer" branch needs a stream whose `write(b"")` raises but whose `write("")` succeeds. `_is_binary_writer` probes with both, so a fake stream also receives the empty-string probe.
+- mypy and Pyright only cover `src` and `tests/typing`. Editor type errors from fake streams in `tests/test_utils` aren't checked in CI.
